# Per-system loader slot overrides
#
# Copy to /media/fat/mister-pat/systems.conf. Read at startup; "Reload library" in the
# settings screen picks up changes without a restart.
#
# Format:   <system name>  <index>  [f|s]
#
#   system name  exactly as it appears in ConsoleMode's section files, e.g. "NINTENDO 64"
#   index        number of the file option in the core's own menu
#   f | s        f = file (default), s = disk slot, used by CD-based systems
#
# Most systems do not need an entry here: the values are built in, read from each core's
# CONF_STR. This file exists for cores that are missing from that table and for unusual
# setups.
#
# Already set as defaults (listed for reference, no need to enter them):
#
#   NES, SNES, NINTENDO 64 and the other cartridge systems   1   f
#   PLAYSTATION                                              1   s
#   NEO GEO CD                                               1   s
#   SATURN, SEGA CD, TURBOGRAFX-16 CD, 3DO                   0   s
#   TURBOGRAFX-16                                            0   f
#
# Still unknown - fill in here once you have tested them:
# CD-I                1   s
# JAGUAR CD           1   s
#
# How to work one out: change the value, choose "Reload library" in the settings, start a
# game. To check without taking over the television:
#
#   mister-gui --no-input --frames 1 --tab games --system NAME --launch-now --dry-run
#
# If a real launch does nothing, the slot matches none of the core's F/S options; the MGL
# playback then aborts silently and the core sits in its own menu. The slot each core
# expects is listed in POC.md.
